---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **나라마다 그 나라 사람이 «실제로 읽은 것» 중 한국 것.** (`/what-countries-read`)
 *
 * ── ⭐ 이 지면만 쓰는 우물 ────────────────────────────────────
 * Wikimedia `top-per-country` — 나라별로 그날 가장 많이 읽힌 문서를 준다.
 * 차트 순위(누가 올렸나)가 아니라 «그 나라 사람이 스스로 찾아본 것»이다.
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 조심하는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 나라마다 «잰 문서 수»가 크게 다르다 — 페루 30장, 일본 4,617장.
 *    몫(%)만으로 줄세우면 목록이 짧은 나라가 억울해진다.
 *    ⇒ **잰 문서 수를 같은 표에 나란히 낸다.** 감추지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 「0」은 «아무도 안 읽었다»가 아니다. «그 나라 하루 상위 목록에 못 들었다»이다.
 * ⛔ 한국 것인지는 눈대중이 아니라 위키데이터로 가른다(P27·P495·P17).
 *    ⭐ 공동제작·이중국적이면 한국이 «여럿 중 하나»다. 그 다섯을 이름째 적는다.
 * ⛔ 터키는 열나흘 다 404 였다. 0 으로 적지 않고 «못 받았다»고 적는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-country-reading.json';

const TITLE = 'What each country actually reads about Korea';
const DESC =
  'Wikipedia publishes the most-read articles per country per day. Over 14 days and 20 '
  + 'countries, 87 Korean articles ever entered one — and 63 of the 93 appearances were Japan.';

const 나라 = [...d.나라].sort((a, b) => b.한국문서 - a.한국문서);
const 일본 = d.나라.find((c) => c.코드 === 'JP');
const 빈나라 = d.나라.filter((c) => c.한국문서 === 0).sort((a, b) => b.본문서 - a.본문서);
const 나온것 = d.나라.reduce((s, c) => s + c.한국문서, 0);
const 못받은나라 = [...new Set(d.못받은날.map((x) => x.나라))];
const 하루도못받은 = 못받은나라.filter((코드) => !d.나라.some((c) => c.코드 === 코드));

const 수 = (n) => (n == null ? '—' : Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 위키 = (p, t) => `https://${p.replace('.wikipedia', '')}.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(String(t).split(' ').join('_'))}`;
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} page="/what-countries-read">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Wikipedia publishes, for each country, the articles its readers opened most that day.
    We took {d.날수} days of it across <b>{d.나라.length} countries</b>, looked at every one
    of the <b>{수(d.서로다른문서)}</b> distinct articles that appeared, and asked Wikidata
    which of them are Korean. <b>{d.한국으로확정된문서}</b> were — {나온것} appearances in all.
  </p>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Korea reaches the top of one country's reading, and it is Japan</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Country</th><th>Distinct articles measured</th><th>Korean ones</th><th>Share of reads</th><th>Most-read Korean article</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {나라.map((c) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{c.이름}</td>
            <td>{수(c.본문서)}</td>
            <td><b>{c.한국문서}</b></td>
            <td>{c.몫 === null ? '—' : `${c.몫}%`}</td>
            <td>{c.무엇[0] ? c.무엇[0].이름 ?? c.무엇[0].제목 : '—'}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Read the second column before the fourth.</b> The number of distinct articles that
      reach a country's daily list varies enormously — {수(d.나라.find((c) => c.코드 === 'PE')?.본문서)} for
      Peru against {수(일본?.본문서)} for Japan — so a share computed over a short list is a
      far weaker measurement than one computed over a long list. Poland is the strongest of
      the zeroes: {수(d.나라.find((c) => c.코드 === 'PL')?.본문서)} distinct articles measured
      and not one of them Korean.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>What Japan reads, in order — the top {일본?.무엇.length} of {일본?.한국문서}</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Article</th><th>Reads over {일본?.잰날수} days</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {(일본?.무엇 ?? []).map((w) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(w.프로젝트, w.제목)} rel="noopener">{w.이름 ?? w.제목}</a></td>
            <td>{수(w.열람)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Japanese Wikipedia is where Korean drama and K-pop are looked up by name — the actors,
      the groups, the series. Nowhere else in this table does that happen.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Nine countries where no Korean article reached the list at all</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Distinct articles measured</th><th>Korean ones</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {빈나라.map((c) => (
          <tr><td>{c.이름}</td><td>{수(c.본문서)}</td><td>0</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      A zero here means <i>no Korean article reached that country's daily most-read list on
      any of the days we measured</i>. It does not mean nobody read one. Everything below a
      country's daily cut-off is invisible to this instrument, and for the countries with
      short lists that cut-off is high.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How we decided an article is Korean</h2>
    <p class="note">
      By Wikidata property, never by name: citizenship (P27), country of origin (P495), or
      country (P17) equal to South Korea. That rule admits co-productions and dual
      nationals, where Korea is one country among several, and we name them rather than
      hide them: <i>Human Vapor</i> (Japan and Korea), <i>Bugonia</i> (United States,
      Korea, Ireland), Tomohiro Machiyama (Japan and Korea), Yoshihiro Akiyama (Japan and
      Korea), and Pom Klementieff (Canada, Korea, France).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    {d.이것이아닌것.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
    {하루도못받은.length > 0 && (
      <p class="note">
        <b>Turkey is missing entirely.</b> All {d.날수} days returned no data from the API, so
        Turkey has no row rather than a row of zeroes. {d.못받은날수} country-days were
        unavailable in total.
      </p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where else this leads</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Netflix charts say something quite different. Mexico held <i>KPop Demon Hunters</i> in
      its Top 10 for <a href="/demon-hunters-countries">51 weeks, longer than the United
      States</a> — and no Korean article reached Mexico's most-read list once in the two
      weeks measured here. Watching and looking up are not the same act. On the acts
      themselves, <a href="/group-afterlife">attention halves two months after the peak</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/what-countries-read" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Most-read articles per country — Wikimedia REST API,
      <i>pageviews/top-per-country</i>, all-access, daily, {d.창}. Read counts arrive rounded
      to the nearest hundred and we do not present them as precise. Korean identification —
      Wikidata P27, P495, P17. Collected {d.잰때}.
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
